# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## What this is

The MLAI corporate marketing site — a fully static, content-heavy brochure for three
products (WDBX vector DB, ABI framework, Abbey assistant). Bun + Next.js 15 App Router +
React 19 + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind 3.4. No backend, no database, no API routes:
all content is compiled into static HTML at build time.

## Commands

Use **Bun**, not npm/pnpm/node. Scripts are pinned to `bun --bun` so the Bun runtime
(not Node) executes the toolchain.

```bash
bun install            # install deps (bun.lock is authoritative)
bun run dev            # next dev — local development
bun run build          # next build → static export into ./out
bun run start          # serve a production build
bun run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit (strict) — the primary correctness gate
bun test               # run bun:test suites in tests/
bun test tests/brand.test.ts   # run a single test file
```

There is no separate lint step; `bun run typecheck` plus `bun test` are the gates.
A change is "verified" when both pass and `bun run build` produces a clean static export.

## Hard constraint: static export

`next.config.ts` sets `output: "export"` and `trailingSlash: true`. This is load-bearing:

- **No** API routes, Route Handlers, middleware, `next/server`, ISR, `revalidate`,
  cookies/headers reads, or runtime server code. Everything renders at build time.
- Dynamic/interactive behavior must be a Client Component (`"use client"`) doing work
  in the browser — there is no server to call.
- Prefer Server Components (the default) for everything static; reach for a client
  component only for genuine interactivity. Current client components: `Nav`,
  `HeroBench`, `PublicationIndex`.
- The build output is `./out` (plain HTML/CSS/JS), deployable to any static host with
  zero rewrite rules.

## Architecture

### `lib/brand.ts` is the single source of truth

Every fact, stat, product description, route, FAQ, and copy fragment lives in
`lib/brand.ts` (and longer prose in `lib/content.ts`). Pages and components import data
from here and render it — they do not hardcode content. When changing site copy or
numbers, edit `lib/brand.ts`, not the JSX.

### The provenance contract (the site's signature rule)

Every numeric claim is a `Stat` carrying a `tag: "measured" | "target" | "reported"`:

- `measured` — reproduced on MLAI hardware; harness in repo (● emerald)
- `target` — engineering goal, not yet achieved (○ amber)
- `reported` — figure from a cited research doc (◆ violet)

Numbers render through `<ProvTag>` / `<StatBlock>` so the provenance is always visible.
**Do not introduce an untagged number into a component**, and do not silently promote a
`target` to `measured`. `tests/brand.test.ts` enforces that every `Stat.tag` is a known
provenance value and that color tokens are valid hex. This contract reflects the
external-claim discipline in the global instructions: targets stay labeled as targets.

### The accent system

Exactly three brand accents — `wdbx` (#00D4FF cyan), `abi` (#7C3AED violet),
`abbey` (#10B981 emerald) — defined as the `Accent` type. Each page commits to **one**
accent. Components receive `accent` as a prop and apply color by setting the `--accent`
CSS variable inline (`style={{ ["--accent"]: accentHex[accent] }}`), which the
`.accent-edge` / surface utilities in `app/globals.css` consume. Tailwind also exposes
`text-wdbx` / `border-abi/40` etc. via the `accentText`/`accentBorder`/`accentBg` maps in
`components/ui.tsx`. Keep all four representations of the palette
(`tailwind.config.ts`, `lib/brand.ts` `colors`, `accentHex` in `ui.tsx`, the Tailwind
classes) in sync if a color ever changes.

### Component layers

- `components/ui.tsx` — primitives: `Section`, `Eyebrow`, `StatBlock`, `FeatureCard`,
  `DataTable`, `ProvTag`/`ProvLegend`, `NextUp`, `Footer`. Re-exports `Nav`.
- `components/content.tsx` — long-form layout: `Prose`, `SplitSection`, `DeepDive`,
  `StepList`, `Callout`, `FAQList` (native `<details>`, zero JS), `Glossary`,
  `PullQuote`, `SpecList`.
- `components/Logo.tsx`, `HeroArt.tsx`, `HeroBench.tsx` — identity / hero art.
- `app/**/page.tsx` — one route per directory; 11 content routes + `not-found.tsx`.
  `app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts` are `force-static`. `app/icon.svg` is the favicon.

The `NextUp` cross-link rail appears on every route **except `/contact`** (terminal page).

## Conventions

- Import alias `@/*` maps to the repo root (`@/lib/brand`, `@/components/ui`).
- TypeScript is `strict`; data objects use `as const` heavily — preserve literal types
  when editing `lib/brand.ts` so `Accent`/`Provenance` narrowing keeps working.
- Tailwind theme tokens: `ink`, `panel`, `line`, plus the three accents and `warn`.
  Fonts are CSS variables (`--font-sora`, `--font-manrope`, `--font-jbm`) loaded in
  `app/layout.tsx` with `display: "swap"`.
- Custom utilities (`.surface`, `.surface-hover`, `.accent-edge`, `.brand-seam`) live in
  `app/globals.css` under `@layer components` — extend there, not inline.
- Accessibility is intentional: skip-to-content link in the layout,
  `prefers-reduced-motion` handling, `aria-current` on active nav. Preserve these.

## Content integrity (from global instructions)

This is public marketing copy for a founder-led, pre-seed company. Do not inflate
maturity, team size, traction, partnerships, or benchmarks. Leadership/team copy lists
only Donald Filimon unless a repo artifact says otherwise. The Apple framing in
`company.appleFraming` is deliberately worded ("built on Apple's public frameworks") and
must not be upgraded to partnership language. Frame unproven metrics as `target`.

## Docs

`docs/01..06` are the design-system, brand-guidelines, brand-voice, brand-review,
system-design, and design-handoff specs the build is verified against.
`ARCHITECTURE-VERIFICATION.md` (repo root) is a read-only audit mapping every route and
component back to those docs — consult it for the full route/component inventory.
